# core/data/talk/grammar/en/cool_extra.tlk - sarcasm and brush-offs with a topic, a memory or a
# relationship (owner: TK; T5b package T5B-COOL). The topic is named only as a plain filler (the
# generator's concept filter keeps unsafe words out). Clean in any room, no register word.
# Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

# ---- with the topic ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.insult.c_x act: dismiss
  "Insult me about {x} all you like. I've heard worse from {x}."
  "Oh, so now it's about {x}? Pick a lane, you menace."
  "Funny, you only get snippy when {x} comes up."
@rule core.criticize.c_x act: complain
  "I'm sorry, but you're not an expert on {x}. I am. Mostly."
  "Don't blame {x}! It's not {x}'s fault. It's yours."
@rule core.tease.c_x act: tease
  "Says the one who's all fluster about {x}. Cute."
  "Ooh, touchy about {x}? I'll be using that later."
@rule core.mock.c_x act: dismiss
  "Mock {x} all you want. {x:cap} won't mind. It's a good sport."
@rule core.complain.c_x act: agree
  "Ugh, {x}! Don't get me started. It's been a whole week."
  "Right? {x:cap} is the worst. Somebody's got to say it."
@rule core.blame.c_x act: disagree
  "Blame {x} if you want. {x:cap} can take it, I can't."
@rule core.dismiss.c_x act: tease
  "So much for {x}. You've got a short attention span, you."
@rule core.threaten.c_x act: dismiss
  "Threatening me over {x}? That's the silliest thing I've heard."

# ---- with a memory of rudeness today ------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.insult.c_memory guard: fact.insulted act: dismiss
  "Another one? You're getting lazy. Where's the flair?"
  "That's your third insult. I'd give you a prize, but no."
  "You're on a roll today. Don't pull a muscle."
@rule core.insult.c_memory_kind guard: fact.insulted act: complain
  "You keep being mean. Did something happen? You can tell me."
  "That's the second time today. Are you okay? Really?"
@rule core.mock.c_memory guard: fact.insulted act: complain
  "First you insult me, then you mock me. What's next, a tax?"
@rule core.tease.c_memory guard: fact.insulted act: tease
  "Aren't you the nasty one today. I like you better like that."
@rule core.threaten.c_memory guard: fact.insulted act: dismiss
  "Rude AND scary? You're stuffing a lot into one visit."
@rule core.complain.c_memory guard: fact.complimented act: tease
  "I thought you were nice earlier. Who stole your good mood?"
@rule core.dismiss.c_memory guard: fact.complimented act: complain
  "You were being nice to me ten minutes ago. What changed?"

# ---- by relationship ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.insult.c_best guard: rel=best act: laugh
  "You did NOT just say that. {.}Okay, I deserved it. Carry on."
  "Only my best friend gets to be this rude. It's an honour."
@rule core.tease.c_best guard: rel=best act: tease
  "Oh, we're roasting? Good. I've saved ten years of material."
  "You think you can out-tease me? I know all your secrets."
@rule core.criticize.c_best guard: rel=best act: agree
  "Ugh, you're right. That's why you're my best friend. Annoyingly."
@rule core.blame.c_best guard: rel=best act: apologize
  "Okay, okay, it was me. Don't be mad. I'll make it up with cake."
@rule core.dismiss.c_best guard: rel=best act: complain
  "Hey, don't brush me off. I'm your favourite. It's in writing."
@rule core.threaten.c_best guard: rel=best act: laugh
  "Ha, you'd never. You're way too soft. You cried at the ducks."
@rule core.complain.c_best guard: rel=best act: comfort
  "Come on, let's go for a walk and moan properly. My treat."
@rule core.insult.c_stranger guard: rel=stranger act: complain
  "We've only just met! That's rude! I'd say something, but we've just met."
  "Wow. Fast. I usually get a bit of small talk first."
@rule core.dismiss.c_stranger guard: rel=stranger act: complain
  "I barely know you and I'm already dismissed. Impressive speed."
@rule core.threaten.c_stranger guard: rel=stranger act: complain
  "Hello to you too. A threat, how welcoming. Do you want a seat?"
@rule core.insult.c_rival guard: rel=rival&!kid_present act: dismiss
  "Predictable. You'd insult a sunrise if it got up before you."
@rule core.blame.c_rival guard: rel=rival act: blame
  "Of course you'd say it's me. You'd blame the moon if you could reach."
@rule core.criticize.c_rival guard: rel=rival act: dismiss
  "Your opinion on me is like a bad coat: nobody asked and it itches."
@rule core.mock.c_rival guard: rel=rival&!kid_present act: insult
  "Mock me? You couldn't mimic a clock. Just ticks, no hands."

# ---- by time of day -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.insult.c_night guard: night act: complain
  "At this hour? Be mean in the morning. I'm too sleepy to defend myself."
@rule core.complain.c_night guard: night act: sympathize
  "Late-night grumbles are the best ones. Pull up a chair."
@rule core.dismiss.c_night guard: night act: joke
  "Fine, ignore me. The moon's up. It's a better listener anyway."
@rule core.threaten.c_night guard: night act: laugh
  "A night threat! How spooky. I'll go and find my sheet."
@rule core.blame.c_night guard: night act: disagree
  "At this hour? I've been asleep, possibly. With my eyes open."

# ---- the spooky household ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.insult.c_ghost guard: ghost act: joke
  "Ooh, an insult! I'm dead, but I feel it. A bit, through the walls."
@rule core.threaten.c_ghost guard: ghost act: laugh
  "Threaten a ghost? Ha, you can't hurt me. I'm see-through."
@rule core.insult.c_hellborn guard: hellborn act: laugh
  "Ha! Back home they'd call that a sweet nothing. Get meaner."
@rule core.threaten.c_hellborn guard: hellborn act: joke
  "That's all? My cousin once glared a bishop into a puddle. Cartoon puddle."
@rule core.mock.c_possessed guard: possessed act: complain
  "Hey! That's not me, that's the other me. We're sharing today."

# ---- stance on the topic -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.criticize.c_pro guard: stance=pro act: disagree
  "I love it, and I'll keep loving it. You can't talk me out."
@rule core.criticize.c_con guard: stance=con act: agree
  "Ha, you're right. I don't like it either. We've got taste."
@rule core.complain.c_pro guard: stance=pro act: disagree
  "Really? I think it's lovely. Maybe you're having a bad day."
@rule core.complain.c_con guard: stance=con act: agree
  "Yes! I can't stand it either. Finally someone gets it."
@rule core.mock.c_neutral guard: stance=neutral act: laugh
  "Ha, okay. I've no strong feelings. It's a funny impression, though."
